  "schema": "prime-filtering-seed-cases-exact-v1",
  "scope": "For positive natural speed lists, each canonical 7-adic level at most a cutoff r has at most three distinct speeds and the family above r has at most five distinct speeds. The proved five-speed bound supplies a sufficiently fine coprime seed; partial filtering yields an actual full-family Modular.Witness, real loneliness at least 1/7, and universal preservation of higher seeded residues. The exponent is chosen with r < m; repeated speeds and an empty higher family are allowed. For at most six distinct positive speeds, an attained minimum level of size at most three is covered. A strict counterexample with actual value < 1/7 must have exactly six distinct speeds and an attained minimum-level/higher-level split exactly 4+2 or 5+1. These two dense cases remain unproved in this component; the unrestricted six-speed runner theorem is not claimed.",
